      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, so the \"dependency\" and \"stifled innovation\" points are pretty standard. but if you're looking at the actual logic, wouldn't you say the whole system is fundamentally flawed because it relies on a level of economic growth that's becoming impossible in a globalized market? i mean, isn't the whole model basically built on a premise that doesn't hold up anymore? how can they justify it?",
